title: Instructions/import_html_wiki

Stages a single-file HTML wiki for import. Loads tiddlers from the file into the in-memory wiki, classifies them, proposes `$:/config/FileSystemPaths` rules, and writes the analysis to `$:/temp/mcp/html-import`. No tiddler file is written yet, only `tiddlywiki.info` when standard plugins were found: call `extract_html_wiki` to commit.

|!Parameter |!Required |!Description |
|`path` |yes |Path to the `.html` single-file wiki to import |

''Behaviour:''

* The call refuses when the wiki already holds content tiddlers (any title outside `$:/`), or while another import is pending. Paths with a dot-prefixed folder or file name (e.g. `.ssh/`, `.env`) are refused too.
* Only one staged import can be pending at a time; calling again while pending refuses with a pointer to the existing one. To discard a staged import, delete `$:/temp/mcp/html-import`.
* Library plugins detected in the HTML file are added to `tiddlywiki.info` by name — they don't need to be extracted as tiddlers and will be loaded by the boot process after the next server restart.
* Sets `Import — Proposed Folder Structure` as the default tiddler so the user sees the proposed rules in the browser.

''Example prompts:''

* "Import the wiki at ~/Downloads/notes.html"

''Workflow:'' see [[Single-File Import]] for the full review-and-commit walkthrough.
